# Docker build context for pickvedio-core.
#
# Only these paths are actually COPYed into the image:
#   pyproject.toml  README.md  prompts/  src/  service/  deploy/healthcheck.py
# Everything below is excluded so the context stays small and so local junk
# (venvs, downloaded video, secrets) can never leak into an image layer.
#
# WARNING: `COPY` in the Dockerfile is explicit, so being listed here is not
# the same as being required. If a future Dockerfile needs another path, delete
# it from this file first. Two paths must stay in the context or the build
# breaks / silently loses behaviour:
#   README.md         -> pyproject.toml declares `readme = "README.md"`
#   prompts/*.md      -> PVC_PROMPT_DIR overrides; the blanket `*.md` rule below
#                        would otherwise drop them (hence the negation)

# ---- git / CI / tooling ----
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.railwayignore
.github
.editorconfig

# ---- python noise ----
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/
env/
.python-version
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
coverage.xml
htmlcov/

# ---- local runtime artifacts ----
pickvedio-work/
*.sqlite3
*.db
*.log
.env
.env.*

# deploy/env.example is a documented template, not a secret: it stays in the
# context (and in git).

# ---- downloaded media / generated reports (ASR path leftovers) ----
*.mp4
*.mkv
*.webm
*.m4s
*.m4a
*.mp3
*.wav
*.flac
*.ogg
*.opus
*.ts
cookies.txt
*.cookies.txt

# ---- not needed inside the container image ----
docs/
skills/
tests/
*.md
!README.md
!prompts/*.md

# ---- editors / OS ----
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
